From 611352d6eba75f76a29fd1f566fb87d2fe23e62d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:15:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Add manual conflict resolution to the sync conflicts page

The conflicts page used to be a read-only list that could only open the parent
directory in DocumentsUI, so conflicts always had to be resolved with a file
manager and it was easy to leave the stale copy behind.

* ConflictItem now carries the conflict path or SAF document URI, the derived
  original file name, the original file and the timestamp from the file name;
* ConflictResolver deletes a conflict copy ("Keep original") or replaces the
  original with it and removes the copy ("Use conflict version"), for direct
  storage folders and for SAF folders alike, reporting readable errors instead
  of throwing;
* the redesigned page shows one card per conflict with its folder, timestamp
  and the three actions, asks for confirmation before destroying data, shows
  progress per item and an empty state instead of closing itself.
